div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/981938-c20-is-out-of-editing?p=982068#post982068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's getting close! Matt still needs to approve the edits, the artists need to finish their illustrations, then it's on to layout, proofing, White Wolf approval, and then backers! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, editing is still relatively early in the process. Speaking from my own publishing experience, editing comes at least a month before there's a typeset proof, and the proof comes at least a month before the book goes to print. <br /> <br /> With artwork to be factored in, and the additional complexity involved in proofing a work like this, rather than a novel or whatever, it's presumably going to be at least three months. <br /> <br /> Since everything in publishing takes twice as long as you expect, I'd say we're looking at maybe six months or more. (What can I say? I'm a realist! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10